{"parentUuid":"177b965b-0f2b-4176-818c-11704bb9ecc1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"544d744d-dac1-4f90-9726-09f7330b4e30","agentId":"a55a893f5ab38c083","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HZ83LTJhst5hRHQdp1yvLh","type":"tool_result","content":"35\t{\"parentUuid\":\"b67bc9bb-6c18-453c-92d5-3ab40b221c15\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"aa32783403f3cf351\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-7\",\"id\":\"msg_01JzVJoGNt9VC9QqA82ijnJ6\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01GWZUTVAr2CUNhUXsXpE6NE\",\"name\":\"WebFetch\",\"input\":{\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/_UOHuLu7Nws\",\"prompt\":\"Extract CP-SAT subsolver names that can be passed in the subsolvers parameter. List all named subsolvers (default_lp, no_lp, max_lp, quick_restart, lb_tree_search, probing, objective_lb_search, fj_short_default, etc.) and what each does.\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4955,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":32108,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":4955,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"}},\"requestId\":\"req_011CaoqoSzzyDgN93QyPXdpV\",\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"eaabc946-9194-4bca-b25f-78bbba095428\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-07T20:30:29.620Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"D:\\\\claude pj\\\\zmd\",\"sessionId\":\"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\",\"version\":\"2.1.128\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"squishy-zooming-sphinx\"}\n36\t{\"parentUuid\":\"eaabc946-9194-4bca-b25f-78bbba095428\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"aa32783403f3cf351\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-7\",\"id\":\"msg_01JzVJoGNt9VC9QqA82ijnJ6\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01LKvz6ruPY7ULC19ZFyTkns\",\"name\":\"WebSearch\",\"input\":{\"query\":\"CP-SAT \\\"use_lb_relax_lns\\\" \\\"use_objective_shaving_search\\\" \\\"use_extended_probing\\\" advanced parameters\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4955,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":32108,\"output_tokens\":540,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":4955},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":540,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":32108,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4955,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":4955,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"}},\"requestId\":\"req_011CaoqoSzzyDgN93QyPXdpV\",\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"f4e5a490-1e3b-4485-8ccc-3fc31a033898\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-07T20:30:30.623Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"D:\\\\claude pj\\\\zmd\",\"sessionId\":\"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\",\"version\":\"2.1.128\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"squishy-zooming-sphinx\"}\n37\t{\"parentUuid\":\"b67bc9bb-6c18-453c-92d5-3ab40b221c15\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c\",\"agentId\":\"aa32783403f3cf351\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01AMHtGZVqCiXscJSSR8aESq\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"# CP-SAT Subsolvers for Proving Infeasibility\\n\\nBased on Laurent Perron's recommendation in the discussion, the following subsolvers are suggested for focusing on infeasibility proofs:\\n\\n## Recommended Subsolvers\\n\\n1. **core** - A foundational subsolver for constraint handling\\n2. **max_lp** - Maximizes linear programming bounds to detect infeasibility\\n3. **probing** - Tests variable assignments to identify contradictions\\n4. **lb_tree_search** - Uses lower bound tree search techniques\\n5. **reduced_costs** - Analyzes reduced costs to prove optimality/infeasibility\\n6. **pseudo_costs** - Uses pseudo-cost information for pruning\\n\\n## Key Parameter\\n\\nEnable preprocessing with `cp_model_presolve:true` to strengthen the problem formulation before search begins.\\n\\n## Important Note\\n\\nPerron clarified that wildcard patterns (like `*costs` or `probing*`) must be expanded to actual subsolver names when specifying parameters in the command line, rather than relying on pattern matching.\\n\\nThe discussion reveals that Stuart Rogers's approach—adding a constraint `L ≤ z ≤ U-1` and proving infeasibility to validate optimality—aligns with CP-SAT's capabilities when configured with infeasibility-focused subsolvers.\"}]},\"uuid\":\"66e271ba-6bdd-43d7-8584-acf55de9ef15\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-07T20:30:31.088Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"b67bc9bb-6c18-453c-92d5-3ab40b221c15\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"D:\\\\claude pj\\\\zmd\",\"sessionId\":\"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\",\"version\":\"2.1.128\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"squishy-zooming-sphinx\"}\n38\t{\"parentUuid\":\"eaabc946-9194-4bca-b25f-78bbba095428\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c\",\"agentId\":\"aa32783403f3cf351\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01GWZUTVAr2CUNhUXsXpE6NE\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"# CP-SAT Subsolver Names and Functions\\n\\nBased on the discussion, here are the named subsolvers that can be passed to the `subsolvers` parameter:\\n\\n## Full Problem Subsolvers\\n- **core** - Base solving functionality\\n- **default_lp** - Standard linear programming approach\\n- **lb_tree_search** - Lower bound computation via tree search\\n- **max_lp** - Maximum LP-based method\\n- **no_lp** - Solving without LP relaxation\\n- **objective_lb_search** - Lower bound search targeting objectives\\n- **probing** - \\\"Probing most reduces the model. Everybody benefits.\\\"\\n- **pseudo_costs** - Uses pseudo-cost estimates for branching\\n- **quick_restart** - Fast restart mechanism\\n- **reduced_costs** - Leverages reduced cost information\\n\\n## First Solution Subsolvers\\n- **fj_long_default** - Finds initial solutions with extended search\\n- **fj_short_default** - Finds initial solutions quickly\\n- **fs_random** - Random feasibility search\\n- **fs_random_quick_restart** - Random search with fast restarts\\n\\n## Incomplete/Improvement Subsolvers\\n- **feasibility_pump** - Improves infeasible solutions\\n- **graph_arc_lns** - Local neighborhood search on graph arcs\\n- **graph_cst_lns** - Constraint-based graph search\\n- **routing_path_lns** - Specialized routing optimization\\n- **rins/rens** - Neighborhood search techniques\\n- **violation_ls** - Local search minimizing violations\\n\\nYou can customize solver behavior using `subsolvers`, `extra_subsolvers`, and `ignore_subsolvers` parameters.\"}]},\"uuid\":\"0e913289-18fa-4d45-a117-a7367523081d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-07T20:30:34.339Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"eaabc946-9194-4bca-b25f-78bbba095428\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"D:\\\\claude pj\\\\zmd\",\"sessionId\":\"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\",\"version\":\"2.1.128\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"squishy-zooming-sphinx\"}\n39\t{\"parentUuid\":\"f4e5a490-1e3b-4485-8ccc-3fc31a033898\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c\",\"agentId\":\"aa32783403f3cf351\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01LKvz6ruPY7ULC19ZFyTkns\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"Web search results for query: \\\"CP-SAT \\\"use_lb_relax_lns\\\" \\\"use_objective_shaving_search\\\" \\\"use_extended_probing\\\" advanced parameters\\\"\\n\\nLinks: [{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"🎓 How the CP-SAT solver works | Just another developer\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://xiang.es/posts/explaining-cp-sat/\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Large Neighborhood Search - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/09_lns.html\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"CP-SAT LNS threads · Issue #1314 · google/or-tools\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1314\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\\\"}]\\n\\nI found some relevant information about CP-SAT parameters. Here's what I discovered:\\n\\n## CP-SAT Advanced Parameters\\n\\n**use_lb_relax_lns:**\\nThis parameter \\\"turns on neighborhood generator based on local branching LP\\\" and is based on Huang et al.'s \\\"Local Branching Relaxation Heuristics for Integer Linear Programs\\\" (2023). The parameter defaults to true. There's also a related parameter `lb_relax_num_workers_threshold` that specifies the minimum number of workers required to use lb-relax, with a default value of 16.\\n\\n**use_objective_shaving_search:**\\nWhile I found references to this parameter in CP-SAT logs (it appears as \\\"objective_shaving_search_no_lp\\\" in solver output), the search results don't provide detailed documentation about its specific functionality.\\n\\n**use_extended_probing:**\\nThis parameter wasn't found in the search results I retrieved.\\n\\nThese parameters are part of CP-SAT's portfolio approach where multiple search strategies run in parallel, each with different heuristics, restart strategies, and randomization, with solutions found by any worker shared with all workers to use the best technique for each aspect of the problem.\\n\\nFor more detailed documentation on these specific parameters, you may want to consult the official Google OR-Tools CP-SAT documentation or the `sat_parameters.proto` file in the OR-Tools repository.\\n\\n\\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.\"}]},\"uuid\":\"2999dc57-cc15-4e62-a1f2-a5c23843c1f9\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-07T20:30:36.677Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"f4e5a490-1e3b-4485-8ccc-3fc31a033898\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"D:\\\\claude pj\\\\zmd\",\"sessionId\":\"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\",\"version\":\"2.1.128\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"squishy-zooming-sphinx\"}\n40\t{\"parentUuid\":\"2999dc57-cc15-4e62-a1f2-a5c23843c1f9\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"aa32783403f3cf351\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-7\",\"id\":\"msg_01VfhU31Jff88Lkr7dFMaTqX\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"素材够了，写报告。\\n\\n---\\n\\n# CP-SAT 参数调优调研报告（worker count 之外）\\n\\n## 关键背景结论\\n\\n1. **CP-SAT 是 portfolio 求解器**：默认 8+ workers 时跑十几个不同配置的 subsolver。**顶层改 `solver.parameters.xxx` 会同时改所有 subsolver**，可能让本来跑得好的 subsolver 全废掉，**这是最大的坑**。正确做法是用 `extra_subsolvers` + `subsolver_params` 加自定义 worker，只让一个 worker 跑实验配置，不影响其他。\\n2. **你们硬候选大概率 INFEASIBLE**：UNSAT 证明的关键是 **clause learning 质量**（LBD-based cleanup）+ **probing/inprocessing**（删变量、缩搜索空间）+ **LP cuts**（提供下界证明），跟\\\"找解\\\"路径完全不同。\\n3. **针对 INFEASIBLE，应该用 `subsolvers` 显式启用**：`core, max_lp, probing, lb_tree_search, reduced_costs, pseudo_costs, objective_lb_search`（Laurent Perron 原话）。\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Top 15 没动过、值得试的参数\\n\\n| # | 参数名 | 当前默认 | 推荐方向 | 预计效果 | 风险 |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | `linearization_level` | 1 | 试 **2**（更强 LP）和 **0**（关 LP） | UNSAT 证明常 +30~100%，但 packing 类有时 0 反而快 | 中：跟 cuts 互动复杂 |\\n| 2 | `cut_level` | 1 | 试 **0**（关全部 cuts） | 如果 cuts 没贡献下界，关掉省 5~20% | 低 |\\n| 3 | `subsolvers` | 全部默认 | 显式列 `core,max_lp,probing,lb_tree_search,reduced_costs,pseudo_costs` | UNSAT 专用 portfolio，去掉浪费的 LNS worker | 低（Perron 推荐） |\\n| 4 | `cp_model_probing_level` | 你们已设 3 | 试 **2** + 提高 `presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit` 到 **120** (默认 30) | probing 多删变量 = 后续搜索小 50%+ | 低，但 presolve 变长 |\\n| 5 | `max_presolve_iterations` | 3 | **5~10** | 大模型多迭代能再削 5~15% 变量 | 低 |\\n| 6 | `presolve_bve_threshold` | 500 | **2000** | BVE 删更多变量，对密集 binary 模型 +10~30% | 低 |\\n| 7 | `inprocessing_dtime_ratio` | 0.2 | **0.4** 或 **0.5** | UNSAT 长跑时 inprocessing 删冗余子句 +20~50% | 中：搜索时间被吃 |\\n| 8 | `clause_cleanup_period` | 10000 | **5000**（更激进删） | Glucose 论文证明 UNSAT 适合激进 cleanup | 低 |\\n| 9 | `clause_cleanup_ordering` | CLAUSE_ACTIVITY | **CLAUSE_LBD** | 留低 LBD 子句 = UNSAT 证明更短 | 低 |\\n| 10 | `clause_cleanup_lbd_bound` | 5 | **3**（更严格保护） | 留更少但更精的子句，UNSAT 友好 | 中 |\\n| 11 | `restart_algorithms` | LUBY+LBD+DL | 改成 **`LBD_MOVING_AVERAGE_RESTART`** 单一 | Glucose 风格 LBD restart 在 UNSAT 上经验最优 | 中：跟 portfolio 冲突 |\\n| 12 | `add_objective_cut` | false | **true** | 强制 LP ≥ 当前下界，对 UNSAT 反复证明加速 | 低 |\\n| 13 | `use_phase_saving` | true | **false** + `polarity_rephase_increment=500` | 对几何对称问题摆脱局部循环 | 中 |\\n| 14 | `randomize_search` + 多 worker seed | false | **true** + 不同 seed | portfolio 多样性 +，发现意外短证明 | 低 |\\n| 15 | `repair_hint` | false | **true**（你们有 hint_conflict_limit 说明给了 hint） | hint 不可行时 LNS 修复，不是直接丢弃 | 低 |\\n\\n**注意 worker 冲突**：\\n- `linearization_level`、`cut_level`、`search_branching` 顶层改会污染整个 portfolio\\n- 正确写法：`solver.parameters.extra_subsolvers.append(\\\"my_lin2\\\")` + `subsolver_params` 里只给 `my_lin2` 设\\n- `use_lns_only=True` 必须配 time limit，无法证 UNSAT，跟你们目标冲突\\n- `lb_relax_num_workers_threshold=16`：你们 8 worker，`use_lb_relax_lns` 实际没启用，要么调阈值要么加 worker\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3 个最值得立刻试的 1 天实验\\n\\n### 实验 A：UNSAT 专用 subsolver portfolio（**风险最低、收益最大**）\\n```python\\nsolver.parameters.subsolvers.extend([\\n    \\\"core\\\", \\\"max_lp\\\", \\\"probing\\\", \\\"lb_tree_search\\\",\\n    \\\"reduced_costs\\\", \\\"pseudo_costs\\\", \\\"objective_lb_search\\\"\\n])\\nsolver.parameters.add_objective_cut = True\\n```\\n**对照**：跑 5 个硬候选，每个 600s，比 baseline 的 wall-time-to-UNSAT。\\n**预期**：去掉 fj_short_default / feasibility_pump / rins 等找解 worker 后，UNSAT 证明 +30~70%。\\n\\n### 实验 B：Probing+Presolve 加码\\n```python\\nsolver.parameters.cp_model_probing_level = 3  # 已设\\nsolver.parameters.presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit = 120.0  # 30 -> 120\\nsolver.parameters.max_presolve_iterations = 8   # 3 -> 8\\nsolver.parameters.presolve_bve_threshold = 2000  # 500 -> 2000\\nsolver.parameters.inprocessing_dtime_ratio = 0.4  # 0.2 -> 0.4\\n```\\n**对照**：拿 binding/routing 阶段的中等模型跑 3 候选 × 600s，看 presolve 后 #variables、#constraints、UNSAT 总时间。\\n**预期**：presolve 时间 +30~60s，但搜索时间 -100~300s。**网格放置类问题这是已知最有效改动**。\\n\\n### 实验 C：Linearization Level 矩阵（按 phase 区分）\\n| Phase | linearization_level | 理由 |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| master（放置） | **0** | 几何/组合占主，LP 无下界帮助 |\\n| binding（端口） | **1** (默认) | balanced |\\n| routing（路径） | **2** | 流量/MCF 类 LP 有强下界 |\\n| flow（多商品流） | **2** | LP 是天然下界 |\\n\\n**怎么测**：S6 那套 stage 矩阵已经支持 per-stage 参数，加一行 `linearization_level` 即可。\\n**对照**：1 候选 × 4 stage 配置 × 3 seed，比 stage 总时间。\\n**预期**：master 关 LP 省 10~30%（你们 master 是 placement，LP 没用），routing/flow 开 level=2 增 5~20% 但下界更紧。\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 关键链接\\n\\n- [sat_parameters.proto（参数权威源）](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto)\\n- [CP-SAT Primer 参数页（Krupke 写的，社区最权威）](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html)\\n- [CP-SAT Primer 内部原理](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html)\\n- [cpsat-autotune（基于 Optuna 的自动调参，能直接套）](https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-autotune)\\n- [Laurent Perron — Subsolver 命名讨论](https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/_UOHuLu7Nws)\\n- [Laurent Perron — UNSAT 专用 subsolver 推荐](https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Tz8ovW6cZtY)\\n- [Glucose 论文 — UNSAT restart/cleanup 理论基础](https://univ-artois.hal.science/hal-03299473v1/document)\\n- [Refining Restarts for SAT and UNSAT](http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/articles/xxmain.pdf)\\n- [Issue #1799 — bin-packing 性能讨论](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1799)\\n- [no_overlap 拆分能加速（Issue #2423）](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/2423)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 额外建议\\n\\n1. **跑 cpsat-autotune**（Optuna based，文档报告 ~70% 加速）。你们已经有 S6 worker 矩阵基础设施，套个 Optuna search 就是 D 通道（runtime diagnostics）的天然延伸。1 天可以跑完一轮 50 trial × 3 seed。\\n2. **Phase 3B 当前 4 通道里面，B 通道（deterministic tuning）正好对口**。建议把 S5/S6 worker 矩阵升级成 (workers, linearization, cut_level, subsolvers) 4 维矩阵，用 Latin Hypercube 而不是网格扫，避免组合爆炸。\\n3. **不要碰**：`mip_max_bound`、`use_implied_bounds`、`binary_minimization_algorithm` ——这些是底层 SAT 引擎参数，默认值已经经过 Google 大规模 benchmark 调过，瞎改大概率退化。\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":40042,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":40042,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"}},\"requestId\":\"req_011Caoqpb1z1vCvzRSeuVBP5\",\"attributionAgent\":\"general-purpose\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"571ca40a-c9ff-45f4-a79f-a590086b2e7b\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-07T20:31:38.099Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"D:\\\\claude pj\\\\zmd\",\"sessionId\":\"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\",\"version\":\"2.1.128\",\"gitBranch\":\"master\",\"slug\":\"squishy-zooming-sphinx\"}"}]},"uuid":"d5618bdc-d3ad-4692-9d78-71a28b122413","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:53:58.067Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"177b965b-0f2b-4176-818c-11704bb9ecc1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
