{"parentUuid":"c06ae3a4-c656-400d-9590-048168426c3f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a55a893f5ab38c083","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Fhyt25u5WM1ghziacavFAk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X1CvBmQb6jUtnZY2RreocV","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/or-tools/v9.15/ortools/sat/cp_model_solver_helpers.cc","prompt":"Find code that registers/launches subsolvers. Specifically:\n1. Where is the list of subsolvers built (search for \"FullProblemSolveLauncher\", \"FullSolveLauncher\", \"SubsolverNameFilter\", \"default_subsolver\", \"subsolver_name\", \"FilterSubsolvers\", or similar).\n2. Is there a special path for problems with objective vs feasibility? Find branches checking has_objective() or model_proto.has_objective().\n3. Find the list of named subsolvers (e.g. \"core\", \"default_lp\", \"max_lp\", \"lb_tree_search\", \"probing\", \"objective_lb_search\", \"pseudo_costs\", \"reduced_costs\", \"quick_restart\", \"no_lp\", \"objective_shaving\"). For each, quote the line where its name is registered.\n4. How does num_workers interact with subsolver count? Find code for \"GetNamedParameters\" or where workers are allocated to subsolvers.\n5. Does specifying an explicit subsolvers list disable LNS workers automatically?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26932,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":1082,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":26932},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1082,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26932,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":26932,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Cap2m94UNyFhD4XYFHXxg","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"67fa8bce-0184-47df-9f4d-e675b958e128","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:54:23.948Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"67fa8bce-0184-47df-9f4d-e675b958e128","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"92127b70-81bc-4e62-9793-d98258588d2b","agentId":"a55a893f5ab38c083","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X1CvBmQb6jUtnZY2RreocV","type":"tool_result","content":"# Analysis of Subsolver Registration and Launch\n\nBased on the provided code excerpt, I can offer limited findings:\n\n## What's Present in This File\n\nThis file (`cp_model_solver_helpers.h`) contains helper functions for loading and solving CP models, but **does not contain the subsolver registration or launch logic** you're seeking.\n\nThe file includes:\n- `LoadCpModel()` - loads a single model instance\n- `SolveLoadedCpModel()` - solves an already-loaded model\n- `AdaptGlobalParameters()` - adjusts parameters based on configuration\n\n## Key Observable Patterns\n\n**Objective vs. Feasibility branching:** The code shows distinct paths:\n```cpp\nif (!model_proto.has_objective()) {\n    // Decision problem path\n} else {\n    // Optimization problem path\n}\n```\n\n**Worker configuration:** In `AdaptGlobalParameters()`, the code determines worker count and related settings like `shared_tree_num_workers`, but this file doesn't show subsolver allocation logic.\n\n**Shared classes registration:** The `SharedClasses` struct registers shared resources (bounds, clauses, LP solutions) across workers, but subsolver enumeration happens elsewhere.\n\n## What's Missing\n\nThe subsolver registry, filtering, and launching code (search for files containing \"FullProblemSolveLauncher\", \"SubsolverNameFilter\", or subsolver name lists) is **not present in this excerpt**. You would need to examine other source files, likely in a higher-level solver orchestration module, to find:\n\n1. The named subsolver list and registration\n2. `FilterSubsolvers()` or similar filtering logic\n3. How `num_workers` maps to subsolver instantiation\n4. Whether explicit subsolver specifications disable LNS workers"}]},"uuid":"e88d89a7-6c22-4001-a99d-939facf72728","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:54:31.444Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"67fa8bce-0184-47df-9f4d-e675b958e128","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c06ae3a4-c656-400d-9590-048168426c3f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"92127b70-81bc-4e62-9793-d98258588d2b","agentId":"a55a893f5ab38c083","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YDpMkwTqvewT8VZMp1sb9k","type":"tool_result","content":"# SatParameters Analysis\n\n## 1. subsolvers (and related fields)\n\n```proto\nrepeated string subsolvers = 207;\nrepeated string extra_subsolvers = 219;\nrepeated string ignore_subsolvers = 209;\nrepeated string filter_subsolvers = 293;\n```\n\n**Comment excerpt:** \"In multi-thread, the solver can be mainly seen as a portfolio of solvers with different parameters.\"\n\n## Named Subsolvers from Comment Block\n\nThe documentation lists these subsolver configurations:\n- `default_lp` (linearization_level:1)\n- `fixed` (only if fixed search specified or scheduling)\n- `no_lp` (linearization_level:0)\n- `max_lp` (linearization_level:2)\n- `pseudo_costs` (only if objective, change search heuristic)\n- `reduced_costs` (only if objective, change search heuristic)\n- `quick_restart` (kind of probing)\n- `quick_restart_no_lp` (kind of probing with linearization_level:0)\n- `lb_tree_search` (to improve lower bound, MIP like tree search)\n- `probing` (continuous probing and shaving)\n\n---\n\n## 2. linearization_level\n\n```proto\noptional int32 linearization_level = 90 [default = 1];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"A non-negative level indicating the type of constraints we consider in the LP relaxation. At level zero, no LP relaxation is used.\"\n\n---\n\n## 3. cut_level\n\n```proto\noptional int32 cut_level = 196 [default = 1];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"Control the global cut effort. Zero will turn off all cut.\"\n\n---\n\n## 4. add_objective_cut\n\n```proto\noptional bool add_objective_cut = 197 [default = false];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"When the LP objective is fractional, do we add the cut that forces the linear objective expression to be greater or equal to this fractional value rounded up?\"\n\n---\n\n## 5. cp_model_probing_level\n\n```proto\noptional int32 cp_model_probing_level = 110 [default = 2];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"How much effort do we spend on probing. 0 disables it completely.\"\n\n---\n\n## 6. presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit\n\n```proto\noptional double presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit = 57 [default = 30.0];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"The maximum 'deterministic' time limit to spend in probing.\"\n\n---\n\n## 7. max_presolve_iterations\n\n```proto\noptional int32 max_presolve_iterations = 138 [default = 3];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"In case of large reduction in a presolve iteration, we perform multiple presolve iterations.\"\n\n---\n\n## 8. presolve_bve_threshold\n\n```proto\noptional int32 presolve_bve_threshold = 54 [default = 500];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"During presolve, only try to perform the bounded variable elimination (BVE) of a variable x if the number of occurrences of x times the number of occurrences of not(x) is not greater than this parameter.\"\n\n---\n\n## 9. inprocessing_dtime_ratio\n\n```proto\noptional double inprocessing_dtime_ratio = 273 [default = 0.2];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"Proportion of deterministic time we should spend on inprocessing. At each 'restart', if the proportion is below this ratio, we will do some inprocessing, otherwise, we skip it for this restart.\"\n\n---\n\n## 10. clause_cleanup_period\n\n```proto\noptional int32 clause_cleanup_period = 11 [default = 10000];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"Trigger a cleanup when this number of 'deletable' clauses is learned.\"\n\n---\n\n## 11. clause_cleanup_ordering\n\n```proto\noptional ClauseOrdering clause_cleanup_ordering = 60 [default = CLAUSE_ACTIVITY];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"The clauses that will be kept during a cleanup are the ones that come first under this order. We always keep or exclude ties together.\"\n\n---\n\n## 12. clause_cleanup_lbd_bound\n\n```proto\noptional int32 clause_cleanup_lbd_bound = 59 [default = 5];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"All the clauses with a LBD (literal blocks distance) lower or equal to this parameters will always be kept.\"\n\n---\n\n## 13. restart_algorithms\n\n```proto\nrepeated RestartAlgorithm restart_algorithms = 61;\noptional string default_restart_algorithms = 70 [default = \"LUBY_RESTART,LBD_MOVING_AVERAGE_RESTART,DL_MOVING_AVERAGE_RESTART\"];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"The restart strategies will change each time the strategy_counter is increased.\"\n\n---\n\n## 14. use_phase_saving\n\n```proto\noptional bool use_phase_saving = 44 [default = true];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"If this is true, then the polarity of a variable will be the last value it was assigned to, or its default polarity if it was never assigned since the call to ResetDecisionHeuristic().\"\n\n---\n\n## 15. polarity_rephase_increment\n\n```proto\noptional int32 polarity_rephase_increment = 168 [default = 1000];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"If non-zero, then we change the polarity heuristic after that many number of conflicts in an arithmetically increasing fashion.\"\n\n---\n\n## 16. randomize_search\n\n```proto\noptional bool randomize_search = 103 [default = false];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"Randomize fixed search.\"\n\n---\n\n## 17. repair_hint\n\n```proto\noptional bool repair_hint = 167 [default = false];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"If true, the solver tries to repair the solution given in the hint. This search terminates after the 'hint_conflict_limit' is reached.\"\n\n---\n\n## 18. use_lb_relax_lns and lb_relax_num_workers_threshold\n\n```proto\noptional bool use_lb_relax_lns = 255 [default = true];\noptional int32 lb_relax_num_workers_threshold = 296 [default = 16];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"Turns on neighborhood generator based on local branching LP...Only use lb-relax if we have at least that many workers.\"\n\n---\n\n## 19. use_objective_shaving_search\n\n```proto\noptional bool use_objective_shaving_search = 253 [default = false];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"This search differs from the previous search as it will not use assumptions to bound the objective, and it will recreate a full model with the hardcoded objective value.\"\n\n---\n\n## 20. share_objective_bounds\n\n```proto\noptional bool share_objective_bounds = 113 [default = true];\n```\n\n**Comment:** \"Allows objective sharing between workers.\""}]},"uuid":"26918b32-131b-42c8-970b-c230bd00613a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:54:33.399Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c06ae3a4-c656-400d-9590-048168426c3f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
