{"parentUuid":"6be7a886-4e75-4050-ad84-78a03d2c64e5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"92127b70-81bc-4e62-9793-d98258588d2b","agentId":"a55a893f5ab38c083","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VwgXJZnVKZGrFihjsKnyLR","type":"tool_result","content":"I've reviewed the provided content, which is the `cp_model_solver.h` file from Google OR-Tools. However, **the subsolver portfolio registration code is not present in this excerpt**. \n\nThe file contains:\n- Helper functions like `CpModelStats()` and `CpSolverResponseStats()`\n- The `FullProblemSolver` class\n- The `FeasibilityPumpSolver` and `LnsSolver` classes (conditionally compiled)\n- The `SolveCpModelParallel()` function that **constructs subsolvers dynamically**\n\nHowever, the **named parameter configurations** (like `\"default_lp\"`, `\"no_lp\"`, `\"core\"`, etc.) and the `GetNamedParameters()` function that would return these are **not shown in this excerpt**. \n\nThe visible code shows:\n```cpp\nconst auto name_to_params = GetNamedParameters(params);\nconst SatParameters& lns_params_base = name_to_params.at(\"lns_base\");\n```\n\nBut `GetNamedParameters()` is declared elsewhere and not included in this content.\n\n**To find what you're looking for, you need:**\n- The implementation of `GetNamedParameters()`\n- The implementation of `GetFullWorkerParameters()`\n- The implementation of `GetFirstSolutionBaseParams()`\n- Potentially a separate configuration header or source file\n\nThese functions contain the actual subsolver registration logic with conditional blocks based on `model_proto.has_objective()` and `num_workers`."}]},"uuid":"f5258efd-498c-4b93-b8ef-d54b1c90ef31","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:54:50.305Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6be7a886-4e75-4050-ad84-78a03d2c64e5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f5258efd-498c-4b93-b8ef-d54b1c90ef31","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a55a893f5ab38c083","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Emsr4pLLUuy8K6zFn4yPzt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R972Xy3yp2XrSPaNJys36F","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/or-tools/v9.15/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto","prompt":"Find the LARGE comment block before the `subsolvers` parameter (field number 207) that explains the portfolio behavior. I need the FULL verbatim comment, including:\n1. The complete enumerated list of named subsolvers and their conditions (e.g. \"only if objective\", \"only if there is no objective\", \"only if num_workers >= X\").\n2. Any explanation of what happens when the user sets `subsolvers` explicitly (does it replace the default portfolio? does it disable LNS workers?).\n3. Comments around `extra_subsolvers`, `ignore_subsolvers`, `filter_subsolvers`, and `subsolver_params`.\n4. ALSO find and quote: `interleave_search`, `share_binary_clauses`, `share_glue_clauses`, `optimize_with_core`, `optimize_with_max_hs`, `use_strong_propagation_in_disjunctive`, `mip_max_bound`, `binary_minimization_algorithm` (defaults + comments).\n5. ALSO find the FIRST-SOLUTION subsolvers: do \"fj_short_default\", \"fj_long_default\", \"fs_random\", \"feasibility_pump\", \"rins/rens\", \"graph_arc_lns\", \"violation_ls\" appear in the proto comments? What about \"shared_tree_search\"?\nQuote the actual proto file content."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":629,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3338,"cache_read_input_tokens":40045,"output_tokens":1199,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3338},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":629,"output_tokens":1199,"cache_read_input_tokens":40045,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3338,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Cap2oEs2wvpXiGh1w3Qyj","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"be9c4ded-1179-4719-a2a0-b7dfd36c2ed9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:54:52.804Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"be9c4ded-1179-4719-a2a0-b7dfd36c2ed9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ad22a9fb-f261-42f6-8cfd-17e16e4e8dd0","agentId":"a55a893f5ab38c083","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R972Xy3yp2XrSPaNJys36F","type":"tool_result","content":"# Analysis of SatParameters Proto File\n\n## Large Comment Block on Portfolio Behavior\n\nThe proto file contains this key comment at field 207 (`subsolvers`):\n\n```\n// In multi-thread, the solver can be mainly seen as a portfolio of solvers\n// with different parameters. This field indicates the names of the parameters\n// that are used in multithread. This only applies to \"full\" subsolvers.\n//\n// See cp_model_search.cc to see a list of the names and the default value (if\n// left empty) that looks like:\n// - default_lp           (linearization_level:1)\n// - fixed                (only if fixed search specified or scheduling)\n// - no_lp                (linearization_level:0)\n// - max_lp               (linearization_level:2)\n// - pseudo_costs         (only if objective, change search heuristic)\n// - reduced_costs        (only if objective, change search heuristic)\n// - quick_restart        (kind of probing)\n// - quick_restart_no_lp  (kind of probing with linearization_level:0)\n// - lb_tree_search       (to improve lower bound, MIP like tree search)\n// - probing              (continuous probing and shaving)\n```\n\n**Critical note:** The proto explicitly directs to `cp_model_search.cc` for definitive subsolver details—not all subsolvers mentioned in your question appear here.\n\n## Related Parameters\n\n**`extra_subsolvers` (field 219):** Adds workers at list beginning; **`ignore_subsolvers` (field 209)** and **`filter_subsolvers` (field 293)** accept glob patterns to exclude/include subsolvers.\n\n**`subsolver_params` (field 210):** Allows custom subsolver configuration; referenced by name in fields above.\n\n## Requested Parameter Defaults & Comments\n\n| Parameter | Default | Comment |\n|-----------|---------|---------|\n| `interleave_search` (136) | `false` | \"distribute the work amongst num_workers\" |\n| `share_binary_clauses` (203) | `true` | \"sharing of new learned binary clause between workers\" |\n| `share_glue_clauses` (285) | `true` | \"short glue clauses between workers\" |\n| `optimize_with_core` (83) | `false` | \"core-based approach\" vs \"linear scan\" |\n| `optimize_with_max_hs` (85) | `false` | \"hybrid MIP/CP approach\" using MIP solver |\n| `use_strong_propagation_in_disjunctive` (230) | `false` | \"slower\" but improves lower bound |\n| `mip_max_bound` (124) | `1e7` | \"bound max magnitude of variables\" |\n| `binary_minimization_algorithm` (34) | `BINARY_MINIMIZATION_FROM_UIP_AND_DECISIONS` | \"exploit binary clause to minimize\" |\n\n**Subsolvers not mentioned in proto comments:** \"fj_short_default\", \"fj_long_default\", \"fs_random\", \"feasibility_pump\", \"rins/rens\", \"graph_arc_lns\", \"violation_ls\", and \"shared_tree_search\" do **not appear** in the provided proto content."}]},"uuid":"4f2890cb-76c5-4cd1-877b-28742f39887a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:55:01.592Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"be9c4ded-1179-4719-a2a0-b7dfd36c2ed9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4f2890cb-76c5-4cd1-877b-28742f39887a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a55a893f5ab38c083","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01UKgWqCPq8yt32pML1y7mcr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two critical findings already:\n\n1. **The proto-listed subsolvers DO NOT include `core` or `objective_lb_search`**. The official list in the proto comment is exactly: `default_lp, fixed, no_lp, max_lp, pseudo_costs, reduced_costs, quick_restart, quick_restart_no_lp, lb_tree_search, probing`. The transcript's claimed \"Perron's recommended UNSAT subsolvers `core, max_lp, probing, lb_tree_search, reduced_costs, pseudo_costs, objective_lb_search`\" includes `core` and `objective_lb_search` which are NOT in the v9.15 proto-documented list.\n2. **`pseudo_costs` and `reduced_costs` are explicitly tagged \"only if objective\"** — they DO work for our `max_lex(area, min_side)` problem (which has an objective). So those two are fine for max-objective.\n\nI need to verify (a) whether `core` and `objective_lb_search` exist as actual registered names in `cp_model_search.cc`, and (b) what happens when the user sets `subsolvers` whitelist (does it kill LNS / first-solution workers)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3417,"cache_read_input_tokens":43383,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3417,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Cap2qKSRCXEWYdHr8FBnJ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"92ac73f7-c360-4624-8b44-13f1b4ccf262","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:55:09.514Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"92ac73f7-c360-4624-8b44-13f1b4ccf262","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a55a893f5ab38c083","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01UKgWqCPq8yt32pML1y7mcr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LTBeyV7FmFoQWgWyFi8PY2","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/or-tools/v9.15/ortools/sat/cp_model_search.cc","prompt":"CRITICAL: I need to verify the exact subsolver name registry. Quote source code verbatim with line context.\n\n1. Find the function `GetNamedParameters()` or `GetFullWorkerParameters()` or wherever subsolver names are registered as strings. Quote every `name == \"...\"` or `add_subsolver(\"...\")` or similar string literal.\n2. Specifically: does the name \"core\" exist as a registered subsolver in v9.15? If yes, what config does it get? If no, what is the closest equivalent?\n3. Does the name \"objective_lb_search\" exist? If no, what's the actual name (e.g. \"objective_shaving\", \"objective_shaving_search\", \"objective_lb_search_no_lp\")?\n4. Does the name \"objective_shaving_no_lp\" or \"objective_shaving_max_lp\" exist?\n5. List ALL the named full-problem subsolvers (the strings users can put in solver.parameters.subsolvers).\n6. Find the code path: when user sets `subsolvers` (whitelist), are LNS workers / first-solution workers (fj_short_default, feasibility_pump, etc.) still added, or are they filtered out too?\n7. For the named subsolver \"probing\": does the user-facing string trigger a special cp_model_probing_level / inprocessing config?\n8. Quote any code that does `if (params.subsolvers().empty())` vs the non-empty case."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3417,"cache_read_input_tokens":43383,"output_tokens":974,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3417},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":974,"cache_read_input_tokens":43383,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3417,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Cap2qKSRCXEWYdHr8FBnJ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ae79656a-585b-494e-8ecc-a61332213438","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:55:17.155Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ae79656a-585b-494e-8ecc-a61332213438","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ad22a9fb-f261-42f6-8cfd-17e16e4e8dd0","agentId":"a55a893f5ab38c083","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LTBeyV7FmFoQWgWyFi8PY2","type":"tool_result","content":"# Subsolver Name Registry Analysis\n\n## 1. Function Location & String Literals\n\nThe function `GetNamedParameters()` (lines 1070–1341) registers all named subsolvers. Here are all `strategies[\"...\"] = ...` assignments:\n\n**LP Variations:**\n- `strategies[\"default\"]` (line 1079)\n- `strategies[\"no_lp\"]` (line 1084)\n- `strategies[\"default_lp\"]` (line 1086)\n- `strategies[\"max_lp\"]` (line 1089)\n- `strategies[\"max_lp_sym\"]` (line 1091)\n\n**Core-based:**\n- `strategies[\"core\"]` (line 1099)\n- `strategies[\"core_default_lp\"]` (line 1106)\n- `strategies[\"core_max_lp\"]` (line 1112)\n- `strategies[\"max_hs\"]` (line 1118)\n\n**Tree/Bound Search:**\n- `strategies[\"lb_tree_search_no_lp\"]` (line 1127)\n- `strategies[\"lb_tree_search\"]` (line 1133)\n\n**Objective Search:**\n- `strategies[\"objective_lb_search_no_lp\"]` (line 1141)\n- `strategies[\"objective_lb_search\"]` (line 1144)\n- `strategies[\"objective_lb_search_max_lp\"]` (line 1150)\n\n**Shaving:**\n- `strategies[\"objective_shaving\"]` (line 1160)\n- `strategies[\"objective_shaving_no_lp\"]` (line 1163)\n- `strategies[\"objective_shaving_max_lp\"]` (line 1166)\n\n**Variable Shaving:**\n- `strategies[\"variables_shaving\"]` (line 1174)\n- `strategies[\"variables_shaving_no_lp\"]` (line 1177)\n- `strategies[\"variables_shaving_max_lp\"]` (line 1182)\n\n**Probing:**\n- `strategies[\"probing\"]` (line 1194)\n- `strategies[\"probing_no_lp\"]` (line 1197)\n- `strategies[\"probing_max_lp\"]` (line 1203)\n\n**Search Variations:**\n- `strategies[\"auto\"]` (line 1210)\n- `strategies[\"fixed\"]` (line 1213)\n- `strategies[\"fixed_no_lp\"]` (line 1216)\n- `strategies[\"fixed_max_lp\"]` (line 1219)\n\n**Portfolio:**\n- `strategies[\"portfolio\"]` (line 1225)\n- `strategies[\"portfolio_no_lp\"]` (line 1228)\n- `strategies[\"portfolio_max_lp\"]` (line 1231)\n\n**Quick Restart:**\n- `strategies[\"quick_restart\"]` (line 1238)\n- `strategies[\"quick_restart_no_lp\"]` (line 1241)\n- `strategies[\"quick_restart_max_lp\"]` (line 1244)\n\n**LP & Pseudo Cost:**\n- `strategies[\"reduced_costs\"]` (line 1251)\n- `strategies[\"pseudo_costs\"]` (line 1258)\n\n**Encoding:**\n- `strategies[\"less_encoding\"]` (line 1265)\n\n**Shared Tree:**\n- `strategies[\"shared_tree\"]` (line 1275)\n\n**LNS Variants:**\n- `strategies[\"lns\"]` (line 1294)\n- `strategies[\"lns_base\"]` (line 1304)\n- `strategies[\"lns_stalling\"]` (line 1309)\n- `strategies[\"lns_routing\"]` (line 1315)\n\n## 2. \"core\" Subsolver Status\n\n**YES**, `\"core\"` exists (line 1099):\n\n```c\nnew_params.set_optimize_with_core(true);\nnew_params.set_linearization_level(0);\nstrategies[\"core\"] = new_params;\n```\n\nIt enables `optimize_with_core()` with no LP (`linearization_level(0)`).\n\n## 3. \"objective_lb_search\" Status\n\n**YES**, `\"objective_lb_search\"` exists (line 1144):\n\n```c\nnew_params.set_use_objective_lb_search(true);\nnew_params.set_linearization_level(1);\nstrategies[\"objective_lb_search\"] = new_params;\n```\n\nAlso available: `\"objective_lb_search_no_lp\"` and `\"objective_lb_search_max_lp\"`.\n\n## 4. \"objective_shaving_no_lp\" & \"objective_shaving_max_lp\"\n\n**YES**, both exist (lines 1163, 1166):\n\n```c\nstrategies[\"objective_shaving_no_lp\"] = new_params;\nnew_params.set_linearization_level(2);\nstrategies[\"objective_shaving_max_lp\"] = new_params;\n```\n\n## 5. All Full-Problem Named Subsolvers\n\nUser-facing strings for `subsolvers` parameter:\n\n`default`, `no_lp`, `default_lp`, `max_lp`, `max_lp_sym`, `core`, `core_default_lp`, `core_max_lp`, `max_hs`, `lb_tree_search_no_lp`, `lb_tree_search`, `objective_lb_search_no_lp`, `objective_lb_search`, `objective_lb_search_max_lp`, `objective_shaving`, `objective_shaving_no_lp`, `objective_shaving_max_lp`, `variables_shaving`, `variables_shaving_no_lp`, `variables_shaving_max_lp`, `probing`, `probing_no_lp`, `probing_max_lp`, `auto`, `fixed`, `fixed_no_lp`, `fixed_max_lp`, `portfolio`, `portfolio_no_lp`, `portfolio_max_lp`, `quick_restart`, `quick_restart_no_lp`, `quick_restart_max_lp`, `reduced_costs`, `pseudo_costs`, `less_encoding`, `shared_tree`, `lns`, `lns_base`, `lns_stalling`, `lns_routing`.\n\n## 6. Whitelist Filtering Behavior\n\nLines 1373–1381 show the default subsolver list when `base_params.subsolvers().empty()`:\n\n```c\nif (base_params.subsolvers().empty()) {\n  names.push_back(\"default_lp\");\n  names.push_back(\"fixed\");\n  names.push_back(\"core\");\n  // ... 14 more entries\n}\n```\n\n**When user specifies `subsolvers` (non-empty)**, lines 1382–1388 use that list directly:\n\n```c\n} else {\n  for (const std::string& name : base_params.subsolvers()) {\n    if (name == \"core_or_no_lp\") { /* special case */ }\n    else { names.push_back(name); }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Critical finding:** LNS/first-solution workers are **NOT** added here. They are managed separately (inferred from different code paths). The `subsolvers` whitelist controls only full-problem solvers.\n\n## 7. \"probing\" Subsolver Config\n\nLines 1188–1203:\n\n```c\nnew_params.set_use_probing_search(true);\nnew_params.set_at_most_one_max_expansion_size(2);\nnew_params.set_shaving_search_deterministic_time(0.001);\nstrategies[\"probing\"] = new_params;\n```\n\nIt enables `use_probing_search()` but does **not** set `cp_model_probing_level` here. That remains at base value.\n\n## 8. Empty vs. Non-Empty subsolvers\n\n**Lines 1373–1388 show the branching:**\n\n```c\nif (base_params.subsolvers().empty()) {\n  // [hard-coded default list of 16+ names]\n  names.push_back(\"default_lp\");\n  names.push_back(\"fixed\");\n  // ...\n} else {\n  for (const std::string& name : base_params.subsolvers()) {\n    // Use user-provided names as-is\n  }\n}\n```\n\nEmpty list triggers default portfolio; non-empty list is user-specified whitelist only."}]},"uuid":"245a3d03-a962-486f-91e0-eb177d114cd5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:55:31.654Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ae79656a-585b-494e-8ecc-a61332213438","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
