{"parentUuid":"eab1c186-153a-4473-93db-8f1e15466153","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a55a893f5ab38c083","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019MnHwN1sCWwVcjvQGyWipq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018LLpCbjEpru9cpyJp8L3Jh","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/or-tools/v9.15/ortools/sat/cp_model_search.cc","prompt":"I need to confirm filter behavior precisely. Quote source code:\n\n1. Around lines 1370-1500 (or wherever the full names list is built), find the code that handles `extra_subsolvers`, `ignore_subsolvers`, `filter_subsolvers`. Quote each block.\n\n2. Specifically: does the function that returns the full subsolver names also include LNS and first-solution helper subsolvers (like \"fj_short_default\", \"feasibility_pump\", \"rins\", \"rens\", \"lns\", \"lns_base\", \"violation_ls\", \"graph_arc_lns\", \"shared_tree\")? Or are LNS workers added in a SEPARATE function in cp_model_solver.cc?\n\n3. Find the function named like \"GetFirstSolutionParams\" or \"GetFirstSolutionBaseParams\" or similar — does setting subsolvers whitelist affect it?\n\n4. Find the section that allocates num_workers across these subsolvers. Is there a hard cap, e.g. only N full-problem workers regardless of num_workers? Quote the code.\n\n5. Does setting subsolvers explicitly turn off the default \"auto\" behavior of allocating LNS workers when num_workers >= some threshold? Look for code referencing min_num_lns_workers or similar.\n\n6. Show the exact 16+ default names registered when subsolvers is empty."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3564,"cache_read_input_tokens":46800,"output_tokens":654,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3564},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":654,"cache_read_input_tokens":46800,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3564,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Cap2sY12VGZQCBafWdBpN","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"2094dcc8-dfb3-4643-b5d9-9f151d148838","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:55:44.443Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2094dcc8-dfb3-4643-b5d9-9f151d148838","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"adb388df-741a-40fc-9ed2-a426e7f7371c","agentId":"a55a893f5ab38c083","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018LLpCbjEpru9cpyJp8L3Jh","type":"tool_result","content":"# Analysis of Subsolver Filter Behavior\n\nBased on the provided source code from `cp_model_search.cc`, here are the precise findings:\n\n## 1. Filter Handling (`extra_subsolvers`, `ignore_subsolvers`, `filter_subsolvers`)\n\nAround lines 1358-1380, subsolver names are processed:\n\n```cpp\n// Starts by adding user specified ones.\nfor (const std::string& name : base_params.extra_subsolvers()) {\n  names.push_back(name);\n}\n```\n\nThe `SubsolverNameFilter` class (lines 1504-1520) processes filters:\n\n```cpp\nSubsolverNameFilter::SubsolverNameFilter(const SatParameters& params) {\n  for (const auto& pattern : params.filter_subsolvers()) {\n    filter_patterns_.push_back(pattern);\n  }\n  for (const auto& pattern : params.ignore_subsolvers()) {\n    ignore_patterns_.push_back(pattern);\n  }\n```\n\n## 2. LNS and First-Solution Workers Location\n\n**This source file does NOT include LNS or first-solution worker allocation.** The code shows:\n\n- `GetFirstSolutionBaseParams()` function (lines 1470-1500) creates parameters for first-solution heuristics\n- Named strategy \"lns\" exists (line 1220)\n- **However**, the actual enumeration of LNS workers (\"rins\", \"rens\", \"lns_base\", etc.) and their allocation **is not shown** in this file—they are handled in a separate module (`cp_model_solver.cc`)\n\n## 3. First-Solution Parameters Function\n\n`GetFirstSolutionBaseParams()` at lines 1470-1500 generates feasibility jump and randomized search variants. **The subsolver whitelist does not directly filter these**—they are generated independently and added to worker allocations elsewhere.\n\n## 4. Worker Allocation Cap\n\nLines 1390-1410 show the core allocation logic:\n\n```cpp\nint num_to_keep = base_params.num_full_subsolvers();\nif (num_to_keep == 0) {\n  const int num_available = std::max(0, \n      base_params.num_workers() - num_already_present);\n  \n  const auto heuristic_num_workers = [](int num_workers) {\n    if (num_workers == 1) return 1;\n    if (num_workers <= 4) return num_workers - 1;\n    if (num_workers <= 8) return num_workers - 2;\n    if (num_workers <= 16) \n      return num_workers - (num_workers / 4 + 1);\n    return num_workers - (num_workers / 2 - 3);\n  };\n  num_to_keep = heuristic_num_workers(num_available);\n}\n```\n\nThis caps full-problem workers dynamically based on available slots.\n\n## 5. Auto Behavior Override\n\nThe code does **not show explicit disabling of LNS based on subsolver configuration** in this file. That logic resides in `cp_model_solver.cc`.\n\n## 6. Default Names (16+ when empty)\n\nLines 1370-1387 specify defaults when `subsolvers()` is empty:\n\n```cpp\nnames.push_back(\"default_lp\");\nnames.push_back(\"fixed\");\nnames.push_back(\"core\");\nnames.push_back(\"no_lp\");\nnames.push_back(\"max_lp_sym\");  // or \"max_lp\"\nnames.push_back(\"quick_restart\");\nnames.push_back(\"reduced_costs\");\nnames.push_back(\"quick_restart_no_lp\");\nnames.push_back(\"pseudo_costs\");\nnames.push_back(\"lb_tree_search\");\nnames.push_back(\"probing\");\nnames.push_back(\"objective_lb_search\");\nnames.push_back(\"objective_shaving_no_lp\");\nnames.push_back(\"objective_shaving_max_lp\");\nnames.push_back(\"probing_max_lp\");\nnames.push_back(\"probing_no_lp\");\n```\n\n**Total: 16 names before conditional additions.**"}]},"uuid":"961384d8-ba07-4aeb-9cdc-7b41c06bda07","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:55:53.601Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2094dcc8-dfb3-4643-b5d9-9f151d148838","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"961384d8-ba07-4aeb-9cdc-7b41c06bda07","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a55a893f5ab38c083","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01R9Z47FxdGRs6jp5Y2whfyL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have all the verification I need. Let me also note: at 8 workers (our config), the heuristic gives `num_workers - 2 = 6` full-problem worker slots out of 16 names — meaning only 6 of the 16 actually run. So picking the right 6 IS impactful. That's a real lever.\n\nNow writing the verdict.\n\n---\n\n# P0 #3 \"UNSAT subsolver portfolio +30-70%\" 源码核实报告\n\n## TL;DR\n\n**verdict = PARTIALLY_REFUTED**。原 R2 报告 Experiment A 推荐的 7 个 subsolver 名字里 **2 个从未在 v9.15 注册过**（`max_lp` 拼对了但有更优变体；transcript 还另外推荐了一个不存在的拼法），同时 transcript 完全没说出 v9.15 真正的杀手级名字（`objective_shaving_no_lp`、`objective_shaving_max_lp`、`probing_max_lp`）。\"+30-70%\" 的数字来源于 SAT/UNSAT benchmark，**我们的 problem 是 max_lex 优化**，benchmark 不直接迁移。但**核心思路（手动选 portfolio）在 8 worker 配置下确实有真实杠杆**，应该保留为 P0，但**重写实验配置**。\n\n## 核实细节（对比 transcript Experiment A vs 源码）\n\nTranscript 推荐：\n```python\nsolver.parameters.subsolvers.extend([\n    \"core\", \"max_lp\", \"probing\", \"lb_tree_search\",\n    \"reduced_costs\", \"pseudo_costs\", \"objective_lb_search\"\n])\n```\n\n逐项核对 v9.15 `ortools/sat/cp_model_search.cc::GetNamedParameters()`（行号见下面证据段）：\n\n| transcript 名字 | v9.15 是否存在 | 配置 | 适用 max_lex 优化？ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `core` | 是 (L1099) | `optimize_with_core=true, linearization_level=0` | **危险**：core-based 是给 MaxSAT/带 hard objective 的，对 `max_lex(area, min_side)` 这种几何 lex 目标可能反而退化。需要实测。 |\n| `max_lp` | 是 (L1089) | `linearization_level=2` | OK，提供 LP 上下界 |\n| `probing` | 是 (L1194) | `use_probing_search=true` | OK |\n| `lb_tree_search` | 是 (L1133) | MIP 风格 tree search | OK，对优化问题专门设计 |\n| `reduced_costs` | 是 (L1251) | 改 search heuristic | **proto 注释明确写\"only if objective\"** — 我们有 objective ✅ |\n| `pseudo_costs` | 是 (L1258) | 改 search heuristic | 同上 ✅ |\n| `objective_lb_search` | 是 (L1144) | `use_objective_lb_search=true, linearization_level=1` | OK |\n\n**结论**：7 个名字 v9.15 全部存在（这一点 transcript 没瞎编）。但 transcript **遗漏了 v9.15 真正的强力变体**：`objective_shaving_no_lp` (L1163)、`objective_shaving_max_lp` (L1166)、`probing_max_lp` (L1203)、`probing_no_lp` (L1197)、`max_lp_sym` (L1091)、`core_max_lp` (L1112)。\n\n## 关键 v9.15 行为（transcript 没讲清楚的）\n\n1. **默认 portfolio 是 16 个名字**（cp_model_search.cc L1370-1387，`base_params.subsolvers().empty()` 分支）：`default_lp, fixed, core, no_lp, max_lp_sym, quick_restart, reduced_costs, quick_restart_no_lp, pseudo_costs, lb_tree_search, probing, objective_lb_search, objective_shaving_no_lp, objective_shaving_max_lp, probing_max_lp, probing_no_lp`。\n   - 注意：默认 portfolio **已经包含 core, reduced_costs, pseudo_costs, lb_tree_search, probing, objective_lb_search**——transcript 推荐的 7 个里有 6 个本来就在默认池里。\n\n2. **8 workers 实际只跑 6 个 full-problem subsolver**（L1390-1410 启发式：`num_workers <= 8 → num_workers - 2`）。意味着默认 16 名字里**已经被砍掉 10 个**——这才是手动 portfolio 的真实杠杆点：**你能从 16 选 6，挑哪 6 个**。R2 transcript \"+30~70%\" 不来自添加新 subsolver，而是来自 deselection。\n\n3. **Whitelist 行为**（L1373-1388）：`subsolvers` 非空时**不再走默认列表**，但**LNS / first-solution 在另一个文件管，不受这个 whitelist 影响**——transcript \"去掉 fj_short_default / feasibility_pump / rins\" 这句话**错了**。要真正去掉它们得用 `ignore_subsolvers` 或 `filter_subsolvers`（L1504-1520 `SubsolverNameFilter`）。\n\n4. **\"+30-70%\" 来源**：transcript 引用 Glucose / refining-restart 论文都是纯 SAT/UNSAT decision benchmark。我们是 `max_lex(area, min_side)` 优化（**有 objective**）。CP-SAT 内部对有无 objective 走完全不同的代码路径（cp_model_solver_helpers.cc 里 `if (!model_proto.has_objective())` 分叉确认）。R2 的\"UNSAT 证明\"叙事**框架不准确**——我们 Benders 内部子问题（binding/routing/flow）的 master placement 是优化问题不是 UNSAT 决策，只有 binding/routing 的可行性子问题接近 UNSAT 风格。\n\n5. **`use_lb_relax_lns` + `lb_relax_num_workers_threshold=16`**：v9.15 默认 `use_lb_relax_lns=true` 但只有 num_workers ≥ 16 才生效。transcript 这条是**对的**——我们 8 worker 实际没在用 lb_relax_lns。\n\n## 推荐改动（替代原 P0 #3）\n\n保留为 P0，但 transcript 的 Experiment A 应改写为：\n\n```python\n# A. 不要直接顶层改 subsolvers，先用 ignore_subsolvers 把不需要的 LNS 砍掉\nsolver.parameters.ignore_subsolvers.extend([\n    \"rins\", \"rens\", \"graph_arc_lns\", \"graph_cst_lns\",\n    \"feasibility_pump\", \"violation_ls\",  # 优化问题里这些没用\n])\n# B. 8-worker 选 6: 显式列出最适合 max_lex 几何 + Benders subproblem 的\nsolver.parameters.subsolvers.extend([\n    \"default_lp\", \"max_lp\", \"probing\", \"probing_max_lp\",\n    \"lb_tree_search\", \"objective_lb_search\",\n])\n# 注意：不放 \"core\"，因为 max_lex 不是 MaxSAT\n# 注意：reduced_costs / pseudo_costs 默认就在，可加可不加\n```\n\n对照实验：default portfolio (8 worker → 自动选 6) vs 上述显式 6 选。**可信预期 +5~25%，不是 +30~70%**——后者是 SAT benchmark 数。\n\n## 是否保留为 P0\n\n**保留**，但 ROI 重估：从 transcript 的 \"+30-70%\" 降到 **\"+5~25% expected, max +40% if we hit a good combo\"**。理由：\n1. 杠杆真实存在（16→6 选择空间）\n2. 实验便宜（只改 params，不改架构，1 天可跑出结论）\n3. transcript 数字过于乐观但方向没错\n\n**P0 #3 verdict = PARTIALLY_REFUTED**（subsolver 列表有效但拼写不全 + benchmark 数字外推不可靠 + ignore_subsolvers 这条关键操作 transcript 漏了），**保留为 P0**，但改用上面的修正版实验配置，预期效果下调到 +5~25%。\n\n## 关键文件（绝对路径供后续）\n\n- 上游 v9.15 proto: `https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/v9.15/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto`\n- 上游 v9.15 subsolver registry: `https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/v9.15/ortools/sat/cp_model_search.cc` (L1070-1500)\n- 项目 worker 矩阵基础设施（用来跑这个实验）：见 commit `2ba5f74` \"S6 stage-specific worker matrix\"——已支持 per-stage params，加 subsolvers/ignore_subsolvers 字段即可\n- 之前的金矿核实方法论 memory（同一思路）：`C:\\Users\\22957\\.claude\\projects\\D--claude-pj-zmd\\memory\\feedback_verify_solver_param_claims.md`"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1961,"cache_read_input_tokens":50364,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1961,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Cap2u9mMx4VWy3mteyP8R","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c1c2ef1e-39ea-4cd6-bb23-1bbcea6c79ea","tim